The model's native size is 1536 numbers per chunk.

 dimensions   recall@1   recall@3    index size   of full
         64       70%        70%        24.0 KB       4%
        128       80%        80%        48.0 KB       8%
        256       80%        80%        96.0 KB      17%
        512       90%        90%       192.0 KB      33%
       1024       90%        90%       384.0 KB      67%
       1536       90%        90%       576.0 KB     100%

These vectors are Matryoshka embeddings: the model is trained so that the first
N numbers are a usable embedding on their own. Truncating is not lossy in the
way that throwing away half a normal vector would be — the important information
is deliberately packed into the front.

Which means the size of your index is a dial, not a property of the model.
Extrapolate, because this is where the decision actually lands:

   dimensions    96 chunks    1M chunks    100M chunks
           64        24 KB       0.3 GB          26 GB
          128        48 KB       0.5 GB          51 GB
          256        96 KB       1.0 GB         102 GB
          512       192 KB       2.0 GB         205 GB
         1024       384 KB       4.1 GB         410 GB
         1536       576 KB       6.1 GB         614 GB

At a hundred million chunks, 1536 numbers is 614 GB and 512 is 205 GB —
a factor of 3, and the difference between two quite different pieces
of hardware. Measure the recall you lose before you pay for dimensions you
do not need.
